0.96, 1.59, 1.68, 1.94, 2.09, 2.41, 2.8, 3.39, 3.69]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[3]"], "text": "9,999.75 dollars.", "t0": 12.72, "t1": 16.87, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$9,999.75", "label": "the largest of the ten", "sub": "$99,449.91 in all"}, "emph": ["9,999.75"], "wt": [0.04, 0.51, 0.95, 1.31, 1.68, 2.4, 2.92, 3.1, 3.67]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 17.39, "t1": 19.01, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.3, 0.41, 0.96, 1.16, 1.29]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "City rules ban splitting a purchase to dodge bidding, under any circumstances.", "t0": 19.13, "t1": 23.36, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "order splitting is not allowed under any circumstances"}, "emph": ["any circumstances"], "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.72, 1.0, 1.33, 1.42, 1.86, 1.94, 2.22, 2.67, 2.9, 3.16]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]", "established[2]", "story[1]"], "text": "In 2008, the Controller found 764 order-splitting violations.", "t0": 23.58, "t1": 28.13, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Human Rights Commission", "kicker": "The audited department", "sub": "2008: 764 order-splitting violations citywide"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.17, 0.39, 0.83, 0.91, 1.27, 1.59, 1.85, 2.21, 2.94, 3.74]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]", "established[2]", "story[1]"], "text": "In 2025, it and the City Attorney audited one department, the Human Rights Commission.", "t0": 28.25, "t1": 32.86, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Human Rights Commission", "kicker": "The audited department", "sub": "2008: 764 order-splitting violations citywide"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.3, 1.07, 1.27, 1.5, 1.64, 1.84, 2.27, 2.73, 2.97, 3.68, 3.77, 3.96, 4.17]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]", "established[2]", "story[1]"], "text": "How much splitting?", "t0": 32.98, "t1": 33.71, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Human Rights Commission", "kicker": "The audited department", "sub": "2008: 764 order-splitting violations citywide"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.3]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[3]"], "text": "743,032 dollars.", "t0": 33.71, "t1": 37.18, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$743,032", "label": "of order splitting at the Human Rights Commission"}, "emph": ["743,032"], "wt": [0.04, 0.64, 1.0, 1.61, 2.31, 2.8]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "One 59,473 dollar invoice, for the Golden State Warriors Arena,", "t0": 37.7, "t1": 42.81, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "One invoice", "sub": "$59,473.41, Golden State Warriors Arena"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Six purchase orders", "sub": "five of $10,000, one of $9,473.41"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Paid", "sub": "with no bid"}], "kicker": "Finding 1.2"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.55, 0.94, 1.35, 1.64, 2.3, 2.64, 3.4, 3.47, 3.55, 3.82, 4.03, 4.44]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "was paid through six orders.", "t0": 42.81, "t1": 44.89, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "One invoice", "sub": "$59,473.41, Golden State Warriors Arena"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Six purchase orders", "sub": "five of $10,000, one of $9,473.41"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Paid", "sub": "with no bid"}], "kicker": "Finding 1.2"}, "emph": ["six orders"], "wt": [0.04, 0.21, 0.52, 0.92, 1.36]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[14]", "defense[1]"], "text": "Former director Sheryl Davis said she explained the limit to be helpful, not to avoid bidding.", "t0": 45.01, "t1": 49.4, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the $10,000 limit: to be helpful, not to avoid the competitive bidding process"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.59, 0.93, 1.37, 1.62, 1.77, 2.22, 2.36, 2.61, 2.68, 2.77, 3.37, 3.56, 3.71, 4.03]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]", "established[5]"], "text": "The audit compared it with just four departments. In City data, Human Resources and Police bunch more.", "t0": 49.62, "t1": 54.98, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Prop Q orders between $9,500 and $10,000, July 2020-June 2024", "rows": [["Human Resources", "21.8%"], ["Police", "18.8%"], ["Human Rights Commission", "14.7%"], ["City Administrator", "14.0%"], ["all departments", "6.1%"]]}, "emph": ["Human Resources"], "wt": [0.06, 0.11, 0.37, 0.69, 0.76, 0.91, 1.13, 1.46, 2.29, 2.45, 2.72, 3.17, 3.39, 3.9, 4.07, 4.53, 4.93]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Citywide, just 6.1 percent sit that close.", "t0": 55.1, "t1": 58.11, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Prop Q orders between $9,500 and $10,000, July 2020-June 2024", "rows": [["Human Resources", "21.8%"], ["Police", "18.8%"], ["Human Rights Commission", "14.7%"], ["City Administrator", "14.0%"], ["all departments", "6.1%"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 0.8, 1.04, 1.33, 1.6, 2.15, 2.43, 2.59]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[8]"], "text": "Rolling Stock’s 4 million dollar bid contract for tires ended in January 2022.", "t0": 58.33, "t1": 63.19, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2022-01-31", "to": "2025-11-01", "days": "", "fromLab": "bid tire contract ends ($4,000,000)", "toLab": "new bid contract begins ($3,750,000)", "kicker": "Rolling Stock Inc"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.67, 0.98, 1.3, 1.6, 1.84, 2.23, 2.41, 2.87, 3.24, 3.4, 3.91, 4.18]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[8]", "established[15]"], "text": "The next began in November 2025.", "t0": 63.31, "t1": 65.52, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2022-01-31", "to": "2025-11-01", "days": "", "fromLab": "bid tire contract ends ($4,000,000)", "toLab": "new bid contract begins ($3,750,000)", "kicker": "Rolling Stock Inc, 601 Bayshore Blvd: also on the school board’s agendas"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.32, 0.64, 0.78, 1.18, 1.51]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "In between, order by order, how much?", "t0": 65.64, "t1": 68.2, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2022-01-31", "to": "2025-11-01", "days": "", "fromLab": "bid tire contract ends ($4,000,000)", "toLab": "new bid contract begins ($3,750,000)", "kicker": "Rolling Stock Inc"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.75, 1.04, 1.23, 1.94, 2.09]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[6]"], "text": "3,056,815 dollars.", "t0": 68.2, "t1": 70.76, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$3,056,815", "label": "through 301 no-bid order lines, April 2022-October 2025"}, "emph": ["3,056,815"], "wt": [0.04, 0.52, 0.75, 1.12, 1.31, 2.02]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "Before July 2024, just two of 241 topped 10,000.", "t0": 71.28, "t1": 76.44, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["orders before July 2024", "241"], "b": ["over $10,000", "2: by $48.63 and $3.93"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.6, 0.85, 1.53, 1.79, 2.2, 2.46, 2.59, 2.88, 3.45, 4.06, 4.21]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "By 48.63 dollars, and 3.93.", "t0": 76.56, "t1": 79.83, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["orders before July 2024", "241"], "b": ["over $10,000", "2: by $48.63 and $3.93"]}, "emph": ["3.93"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.44, 0.78, 0.98, 1.45, 1.91, 2.09, 2.32, 2.63, 2.82]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why", "established[1]"], "text": "Year-round buying from one supplier is what a bid contract is for.", "t0": 79.95, "t1": 83.38, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Prop Q is not meant for recurring purchases"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.48, 0.88, 1.14, 1.35, 1.89, 2.05, 2.19, 2.28, 2.48, 2.92, 3.04]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[4]"], "text": "On July 1, 2024, the limit doubled. And the orders?", "t0": 83.6, "t1": 87.43, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "1 July 2024", "kicker": "The limit doubles", "sub": "from $10,000 to $20,000"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.36, 0.79, 0.99, 1.64, 1.75, 2.07, 2.84, 2.91, 3.03]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "19,898.17 dollars,", "t0": 87.43, "t1": 91.62, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$19,912.18", "label": "and $19,898.17: the first two orders, 12 July 2024"}, "emph": ["19,898.17"], "wt": [0.04, 0.46, 1.03, 1.24, 1.6, 2.19, 2.66, 2.91, 3.41]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "and 19,912.18.", "t0": 91.62, "t1": 94.63, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$19,912.18", "label": "and $19,898.17: the first two orders, 12 July 2024"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.18, 0.53, 1.05, 1.23, 1.47, 1.96, 2.47, 2.71]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "established[10]"], "text": "Half as many orders, twice as big, about the same yearly total.", "t0": 95.15, "t1": 98.7, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["FY2024", "86 orders · $851,346"], "b": ["FY2025", "41 orders · $812,844"]}, "emph": ["twice as big"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.24, 0.45, 1.05, 1.37, 1.53, 2.02, 2.27, 2.44, 2.75, 3.1]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "established[10]"], "text": "That suggests the limit